From 3edd79398068fd6ac0ce110a5e1f020dfd51ffe9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:45:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(plugins): load a plugin enabled after boot at the next
 new-session agent build [daveey]

A long-lived process discovered plugins once: discover_and_load returns early once _discovered is
set, and hermes plugins enable nudges only the host-level serve backend and the gateway socket. A
per-profile serve --isolated backend that booted before an enable never registered the plugin's
hooks until it restarted (nine every-host guards stayed out of ten hub backends on 10-30).

PluginManager now keeps the pre-sweep fingerprint (and a cheap precheck) of the inputs it swept.
refresh_if_inputs_changed() re-runs the forced pass load_and_go_live uses (under _GO_LIVE_LOCK +
_discovery_lock) only when they changed. tui_gateway _make_agent and the gateway's
_build_fresh_agent call it before building a new session's agent, never mid-turn. Unchanged
inputs cost one precheck stat pass: median 2.4 ms on the hub's 55-plugin default home.

Also corrects the delegation router comment that claimed the next scan picks such a plugin up.
---
